Q: getting code E401 error after running &#39;npm install&#39; A: <p>I had the same problem. I used a custom <code>.npmrc</code> file in my project's root and forgot to specify the <code>_authToken</code>.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>registry=https://registry.npmjs.org
@hugeicons:registry=https://npm.hugeicons.com/
//npm.hugeicons.com/:_authToken=${PACKAGES_TOKEN}
legacy-peer-deps=false
</code></pre>
<p>Make sure to specify <code>_authToken=</code></p>

Q: Best practice to create IllegalArgumentException exception handler in java spring boot A: <pre><code>@ExceptionHandler({JwtException.class, IllegalArgumentException.class})
public ResponseEntity&lt;ApiResponse&lt;?&gt;&gt; handleJwtError(HttpServletRequest request) {
    return ResponseEntity
            .status(HttpStatus.UNAUTHORIZED)
            .body(ApiResponse.fail(&quot;Invalid or expired token&quot;, null, request.getRequestURI()));
}
</code></pre>
<pre><code>public record ApiResponse&lt;T&gt;(
        Boolean success,
        String message,
        T data,
        String path,
        LocalDateTime timestamp
) {
    public static &lt;T&gt; ApiResponse&lt;T&gt; success(T data, String path) {
        return success(&quot;Success&quot;, data, path);
    }

    public static &lt;T&gt; ApiResponse&lt;T&gt; success(String message, T data, String path) {
        return new ApiResponse&lt;&gt;(true, message, data, path, LocalDateTime.now());
    }

    public static &lt;T&gt; ApiResponse&lt;T&gt; fail(String message, T data, String path) {
        return new ApiResponse&lt;&gt;(false, message, data, path, LocalDateTime.now());
    }
}
</code></pre>
